  "info": {
    "name": "Corenio API — Carts/Orders Test Log v5 (2026-09-01, round 5 — FULL SUCCESS)",
    "description": "Fifth test pass, run after Dave's team's latest merge. Result: FULL END-TO-END SUCCESS for the first time — the complete checkout flow (login -> create cart -> add item -> update quantity -> shipping methods -> set shipping -> finalize -> payment link -> invoice PDF) all confirmed working with real data, including a REAL order placed (order_id 373, abdulzziwa007@outlook.com). Critical change from all prior rounds: item-mutation paths flipped back to the ORIGINAL documented paths (no '/cart/' segment) — the '/cart/' workaround that worked for 3 straight rounds is now broken. Our client code needs updating to match. Also confirmed: finalize leaves orders unpaid (total_paid:0) — paymentlink is required afterward to actually collect payment. Still broken, unrelated to this merge: GET /carts/list (use bare /carts instead). No secrets embedded — fill in corenio_api_key under this collection's Variables tab before running.",
